#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=2008-05-21|author=Rebecca Cathcart|title=A Developer’s Unusual Plan for Bright Lights, Inspired by a Dark Film|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2008/05/21/arts/design/21blad.html
|passage=The area already has plenty of loud billboards and klieg lights that have drawn complaints from some neighborhood groups, so the city is concerned about anything billboardesque. Mr. Astani’s application to build the '''LED''' panels is undergoing an environmental review by city planning officials.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210126113724/https://www.nytimes.com/2008/05/21/arts/design/21blad.html}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Julio Sanchez; Maria P. Canton|title=Embedded Systems Circuits and Programming|isbn=1439879311|page=12
|passage=The light-emitting capacity of an '''LED''' is measured in megacandela [''recte'' millicandelas] or mcd. Small commercial '''LEDs''' range from 10 to about 5000 mcd.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Snap Circuits Light|url=https://www.elenco.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/SCL175-2.pdf|date=2017-10|page=5, 59|work=w:Snap Circuits|publisher=Elenco|passage=In some projects, the fiber optic cable will be mounted on the '''LEDs''' (D1, D6, D8, and on U22) or the phototransistor (Q4). {{...}} Light is transmitted from the color '''LED''', through the fiber optic cable, to control the NPN transistor (Q2) and red '''LED''' (D1).|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250606012953/https://www.elenco.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/10/SCL175-2.pdf}}

