#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=January 21, 2007|author=The Associated Press|title=Adirondacks Are His Life, All 101 Years and Counting|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2007/01/21/sports/othersports/21outdoors.html
|passage=After working briefly for a federal entomologist to control the spruce budworm — and spraying '''DDT''' from the air — he returned to the Adirondacks in 1946 to be district ranger at Cranberry Lake for 11 years.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221126041511/https://www.nytimes.com/2007/01/21/sports/othersports/21outdoors.html|archivedate=26 November 2022}}
